#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
VIDYUT - Visualised Industrial Dashboard for Yield & Utility Tracking
=====================================================================
One self-contained program (Python 3.8+, standard library only).

  python vidyut.py                  start the server  (http://localhost:8080)
  python vidyut.py --passwd admin   change a password
  python vidyut.py --adduser NAME ROLE   (admin|energy_manager|plant_manager|engineer|viewer)
  python vidyut.py --backup         zip config, audit log, events, history and database
  python vidyut.py --import-xlsx ENERGY_TRACKING.xlsx   refresh history (needs: pip install openpyxl)
  python vidyut.py --verify-audit   check the audit-log hash chain

Data: every metering point comes from the built-in EMS list. A meter shows GENERATED demo data
until real readings arrive. Live meters (Siemens PAC3200 over Modbus TCP) are listed in
vidyut_config.json -> "live_meters". As soon as one answers it becomes LIVE; if it later stops
answering it shows OFFLINE (never simulated again until restart).

Security: PBKDF2 passwords, lockout, HttpOnly+SameSite cookies, CSP with nonce, idle timeout,
hash-chained audit log, read-only data path (the program never writes to any meter or PLC).
Run behind HTTPS (set tls_cert / tls_key in the config) when used outside a closed network.
"""
